  "foaf:name": "South East Pacific Ocean Digital Twin",
  "sdo:name": "South East Pacific Ocean Digital Twin",
  "sdo:description": "SEAPOD is a regional initiative to develop an integrated ocean-climate information platform for the Southeast Pacific. It focuses on two complementary components: a regional digital twin dashboard for data visualization and the advancement of regional climate prediction models. Both components are designed to enhance and interconnect decades-long efforts developed under the Regional Study for El Niño (ERFEN) and the GOOS Regional Alliance for the South East Pacific (GRASP) programs. By integrating state-of-the-art digital innovation and AI, SEAPOD aims to match the sophistication of global platforms while delivering regionally tailored ocean and climate information products. The initiative will feature a dynamic, user-friendly dashboard and interactive visualization panel, enabling real-time access to model outputs and decision-ready information with an accessible, user-oriented digital ecosystem improving ocean governance and decision-making through co-designed, science-based tools",
